<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        The <a href="/files">File Manager</a> holds your company's files: images for projection screens and
        courses, music, audio clips, and documents attached to welcome emails. It needs the Admin or
        CanManageFiles role. Staff documents such as right-to-work checks are kept separately and never
        appear here.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Folders">
        <FluentText>
            Folders are on the left. Select one to open it, use the path at the top to go back up, and select
            <strong>New Folder</strong> to add one inside the current folder.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Uploading">
        <FluentText>
            Drag files onto the upload area, or select it to browse. You can upload up to 4 files at a time,
            each up to 100 MB. Audio files (MP3, WAV, FLAC, OGG, AAC, M4A, WMA) are also added to the music library.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            You can upload images (PNG, JPG, GIF, WebP, BMP, SVG, HEIC), video (MP4, M4V, WebM, MOV, MKV, AVI),
            audio, PDFs, Word, Excel and PowerPoint files and their OpenDocument versions, RTF, text, CSV, JSON
            and ZIP files. Other types, such as programs or web pages, are refused.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Managing files">
        <FluentText>Each file has buttons to download, move to another folder, rename (the extension is kept) and delete.</FluentText>
        <HelpNote Intent="MessageBarIntent.Warning">
            A file can't be deleted while it's attached to an onboarding email, or used as an
            audio clip. Delete the clip first. Deleting a music file removes the song from the music library too.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
